6,"quote":"We offer a broad range of products and services aimed at serving the financial needs of our customers. We sell these products to corporations and other institutions (including local, state and federal governments) and their respective employees, as well as individuals.","sentences":[6,7]},{"passage_id":"0001099219-26-000013:1:4","accession":"0001099219-26-000013","item":"1","char_start":16413,"char_end":16811,"quote":"Our Group Benefits segment, based in the U.S., offers life insurance, dental, group short- and long-term disability, paid family and medical leave, individual disability, accidental death and dismemberment (\"AD&D\") insurance, accident & health insurance, and vision, as well as prepaid legal plans and pet insurance. We also sell administrative services-only (\"ASO\") arrangements to some employers.","sentences":[10,11]}],"searches":[{"queries":["principal products services","how we generate revenue","segments","customers","business model"],"items":["1"],"seeded":true,"passage_ids":["0001099219-26-000013:1:5","0001099219-26-000013:1:8","0001099219-26-000013:1:64","0001099219-26-000013:1:4"]}],"llm_calls":1,"tool_calls":2,"stop_reason":"submitted","usage":{"prompt_tokens":2039,"completion_tokens":155,"total_tokens":2194,"reasoning_tokens":0},"actual_cost_usd":0.0,"notional_cost_usd":0.00074225},"critic_status":"passed"},{"finding":{"criterion":"durable_competitive_advantage","verdict":"insufficient evidence","rationale":"The filing describes the industry as highly competitive with low barriers to entry and does not provide concrete, measurable evidence of a durable competitive advantage such as a specific market share, exclusive franchise, or quantified cost position. The company's statements regarding its competitive position are assertions of its strengths rather than evidence of a protected, long-term advantage.","citations":[],"searches":[{"queries":["competition competitive","brand","market share","pricing power price increases","switching costs","patents intellectual property","scale cost advantage","network"],"items":["1","1A"],"seeded":true,"passage_ids":["0001099219-26-000013:1:82","0001099219-26-000013:1A:66","0001099219-26-000013:1:85","0001099219-26-000013:1A:43"]}],"llm_calls":1,"tool_calls":2,"stop_reason":"submitted","usage":{"prompt_tokens":2255,"completion_tokens":176,"total_tokens":2431,"reasoning_tokens":0},"actual_cost_usd":0.0,"notional_cost_usd":0.00082775},"critic_status":"passed"},{"finding":{"criterion":"candid_management","verdict":"not assessed","rationale":"The cited sentence pointers were invalid twice, so no finding is recorded.","citations":[],"searches":[{"queries":["challenges","did not meet","below our expectations","we did not achieve","lessons","write-down of our investment","impairment","material weakness","restatement","decline decreased","we expect headwinds"],"items":["7","1A"],"seeded":true,"passage_ids":["0001099219-26-000013:1A:28","0001099219-26-000013:7:134","0001099219-26-000013:1A:50","0001099219-26-000013:7:146"]}],"llm_calls":2,"tool_calls":3,"stop_reason":"invalid_citation","usage":{"prompt_tokens":5383,"completion_tokens":287,"total_tokens":5670,"reasoning_tokens":0},"actual_cost_usd":0.0,"notional_cost_usd":0.00177625},"critic_status":"passed"},{"finding":{"criterion":"rational_capital_allocation","verdict":"evidence weak","rationale":"The filing lists the primary uses of liquidity and capital, such as debt service, dividends, and share repurchases, and defines free cash flow as cash available for reinvestment or non-mandatory capital actions. However, it does not quantify the actual amounts spent on these specific capital allocation activities during the fiscal year.","citations":[{"passage_id":"0001099219-26-000013:7:226","accession":"0001099219-26-000013","item":"7","char_start":444035,"char_end":444692,"quote":"•The Company uses a measure of free cash flow to facilitate an understanding of its ability to generate cash for reinvestment into its businesses or use in non-mandatory capital actions. The Company defines free cash flow as the sum of cash available at MetLife's holding companies from dividends from operating subsidiaries, expenses and other net flows of the holding companies (including capital contributions to subsidiaries), and net contributions from debt to be at or below target leverage ratios. This measure of free cash flow is prior to capital actions, such as common stock dividends and repurchases, debt reduction and mergers and acquisitions.","sentences":[1,3]},{"passage_id":"0001099219-26-000013:7:207","accession":"0001099219-26-000013","item":"7","char_start":422319,"char_end":423001,"quote":"The primary sources of MetLife, Inc.'s liquid assets are dividends and returns of capital from subsidiaries, issuances of long-term debt, issuances of common and preferred stock, and net receipts from subsidiaries under a tax sharing agreement. MetLife, Inc.'s insurance subsidiaries are subject to regulatory restrictions on the payment of dividends imposed by the regulators of their respective domiciles.\nThe primary uses of MetLife, Inc.'s liquid assets are principal and interest payments on long-term debt, dividends on and repurchases of common and preferred stock, capital contributions to subsidiaries, funding of business acquisitions, income taxes and operating expenses.","sentences":[1,3]}],"searches":[{"queries":["share repurchases buyback","dividends","acquisitions","capital expenditures","return on invested capital","debt reduction"],"items":["7"],"seeded":true,"passage_ids":["0001099219-26-000013:7:226","0001099219-26-000013:7:209","0001099219-26-000013:7:207","0001099219-26-000013:7:208"]},{"queries":["\"common stock\" dividends repurchases 2025 2024 amount"],"items":["7"],"seeded":false,"passage_ids":["0001099219-26-000013:7:194","0001099219-26-000013:7:196","0001099219-26-000013:7:210","0001099219-26-000013:7:209"]},{"queries":["\"common stock\" dividends repurchases \"million\" 2025 2024"],"